  "body": "Stacked on #2310 (merge #2310 first)\n\n## What changed\n\nLinuxCNC, Tormach, and grblHAL now refuse a positive dwell on G73 and G85.\nThe message names the cycle and the requested dwell in seconds.\nThe guard runs before a cycle block or a modal X/Y continuation.\nA zero dwell keeps the existing cycle words.\n\nThe issue commit changes three posts, adds one test file, and records the decision.\nThe LinuxCNC post comes from the parent PR.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe cycle maps select G73 for PECK and G85 for REAM.\nThe output has no P word for these cycles.\nThe old guard checks only G83, so the posts drop the requested dwell without a message.\nThe new guards use the existing G83 refusal format.\n\nReadings: issue #2609, the existing G83 tests, and the cycle handlers in all three posts.\nThe post provenance cites the public LinuxCNC, PathPilot, and grblHAL references.\n\n## Tests\n\nThe new `g73_g85_dwell_linuxcnc` suite has seven tests:\n\n- `tormach_refuses_g73_dwell`\n- `tormach_refuses_g85_dwell`\n- `grblhal_refuses_g73_dwell`\n- `grblhal_refuses_g85_dwell`\n- `linuxcnc_refuses_g73_dwell`\n- `linuxcnc_refuses_g85_dwell`\n- `linuxcnc_family_posts_g73_g85_without_dwell_unchanged`\n\nAll six refusal tests failed on unchanged code. The zero-dwell test passed.\nAll seven tests pass with the fix.\nThe refusal tests also check a later hole and a raw 0.0001-second dwell.\n\nEach mutation restores one old post file.\nThe Tormach and grblHAL mutations use `upstream/main`.\nThe LinuxCNC mutation uses `base-2310` because upstream/main has no LinuxCNC post.\nEach mutation makes that post's two refusal tests fail.\nEach restore makes all seven tests pass.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 641 steps, zero failures.\nThis run includes the inherited parent app and post suites.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green.\n`git diff --check`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone in the issue commit. The diff against `base-2310` has no `.nc` or `.cl` change.\n\nThe required diff against `upstream/main` includes these unchanged parent goldens:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/contour_disc_hole.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/contour_plate_with_hole.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/contour_tangential_lead.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/drill_peck.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/drill_plate.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/face_square_40x40.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/face_square_40x40_stepped.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/pocket_waterline_plate_with_island.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/pocket_zigzag_plate_with_island.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/slot_fullwidth_centerline.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/slot_wide_channel_rows.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/linuxcnc/trace_plate_with_hole.nc`\n- `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/synth_linuxcnc.nc`\n\nThe parent also predates main's change to `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach-lathe/thread_g76_inch.nc`.\nIt predates main's addition of `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.nc`.\nThese two differences appear in the direct upstream diff.\nAll 15 files match the parent branch. This issue changes none of their lines.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo controller simulation or machine run.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n#2310 adds `assets/posts/linuxcnc.cps`, including `onCycle`.\nThis branch starts at its head, `0c17caa79e10a7276ac9814cbf77c08211d7193f`.\nThe new guard changes `onCycle` in that file.\nNo other open PR changes the issue's files.\n\nEffort: high. No escalation.\n\nChangelog: LinuxCNC, Tormach, and grblHAL refuse unsupported G73 and G85 dwell by name instead of dropping it.\n\nFixes #2609\n",
